{
  "dom_id": "step-q127762",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=4\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 3=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=4\\cdot 9-3\\cdot 12=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse.",
